day of the week for Kim's birthday, we need to work backwards from today, which is Wednesday. We need to consider how the days of the week cycle every 7 days and then use the information that 200 days have passed.\n\nFirst, we find the remainder when 200 is divided by 7, because the days of the week repeat every 7 days. This can be done using the modulo operation:\n\n\\[ 200 \\div 7 = 28 \\text{ remainder } 4 \\]\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"Continue from the interruption. Output only the continuation. Do not restart the solution.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"a91c4d30b34963e2b1e28da3c1242e589ba0676312ca25535f4912d82dfb1527"},"seconds":6.635204076766968,"seed":1080035111652442369,"stop":"eos","text":"Therefore, \\(200 \\mod 7 = 4\\). This means that 200 days ago is equivalent to 4 days before today in terms of the day of the week.\n\nNow, we count backwards 4 days from Wednesday:\n- 1 day before Wednesday is Tuesday.\n- 2 days before Wednesday is Monday.\n- 3 days before Wednesday is Sunday.\n- 4 days before Wednesday is Saturday.\n\nSo, Kim's birthday was on a Saturday.\n\n\\(\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}\\)"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"Therefore, \\(200 \\mod 7 = 4\\). This means that 200 days ago is equivalent to 4 days before today in terms of the day of the week.\n\nNow, we count backwards 4 days from Wednesday:\n- 1 day before Wednesday is Tuesday.\n- 2 days before Wednesday is Monday.\n- 3 days before Wednesday is Sunday.\n- 4 days before Wednesday is Saturday.\n\nSo, Kim's birthday was on a Saturday.\n\n\\(\\boxed{\\text{Saturday}}\\)","id":"number_theory:49"}
